---
/**
 * Accessibility statement.
 *
 * Brief §12: "Build the accessibility statement and privacy pages as part of
 * the initial scope, not afterwards."
 *
 * Brief §7 notes a conformance statement is a tangible advantage when bidding
 * institutional and government-linked work.
 *
 * IMPORTANT: this statement must stay truthful. Update the "last reviewed"
 * date and the known-issues list whenever the site changes. A statement that
 * overclaims is worse than none.
 */
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE, CONTACT } from '../consts.js';

const lastReviewed = '[CONFIRM DATE OF PRE-LAUNCH ACCESSIBILITY AUDIT]';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Accessibility"
  description={`Accessibility statement for the ${SITE.name} website, targeting WCAG 2.2 Level AA.`}
>
  <div class="wrap section reveal">
    <div class="prose reveal__item">
      <h1>Accessibility statement</h1>

      <p>
        {SITE.name} is committed to making this website usable by as many
        people as possible, including people who use screen readers, magnify
        the page, navigate by keyboard alone, or rely on speech input.
      </p>

      <h2>Conformance status</h2>
      <p>
        This website is designed to conform to the
        <a
          href="https://www.w3.org/TR/WCAG22/"
          rel="noopener external">Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) 2.2</a>
        at Level AA.
      </p>
      <p>
        Last reviewed: {lastReviewed}.
      </p>

      <h2>What we have done</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          The site works with JavaScript disabled. All content is readable, all
          navigation is functional, and the enquiry form can be submitted
          without JavaScript.
        </li>
        <li>
          Every image carries alternative text describing its architectural
          subject. Purely decorative images are marked so screen readers skip
          them.
        </li>
        <li>
          All text meets a minimum contrast ratio of 4.5:1 against its
          background. Colour combinations are tested programmatically rather
          than by eye.
        </li>
        <li>
          Every interactive element can be reached and operated by keyboard, in
          a logical order, with a clearly visible focus indicator.
        </li>
        <li>
          A “skip to main content” link is the first item in the tab order on
          every page.
        </li>
        <li>
          Expandable panels use the browser's own disclosure control, so they
          are announced correctly by screen readers and work without
          JavaScript.
        </li>
        <li>
          Animation and transitions are disabled automatically for visitors
          whose system is set to reduce motion.
        </li>
        <li>
          Text can be resized to 200% without loss of content or function, and
          the layout adapts from 360px to 2560px wide.
        </li>
        <li>There are no auto-advancing carousels and no scroll-jacking.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Known limitations</h2>
      <p>
        We are not aware of any outstanding accessibility barriers on this
        site. If any are identified, they will be listed here with a target
        date for resolution.
      </p>

      <h2>How this was tested</h2>
      <p>
        Testing combined automated tooling with manual checks, because
        automated tools alone catch only a fraction of accessibility issues.
        Testing covered:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Automated auditing of every page template</li>
        <li>A full keyboard-only pass</li>
        <li>A screen reader pass on the home, project detail and contact pages</li>
        <li>Manual contrast checks on every text and background combination</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Feedback</h2>
      <p>
        If you encounter a barrier on this site, or need information from it in
        a different format, please tell us — we will do our best to help and to
        fix the underlying problem.
      </p>
      <p>
        Email: {CONTACT.email}<br />
        Telephone: {CONTACT.phone}
      </p>

      <h2>Third-party content</h2>
      <p>
        Our enquiry form is processed by a third-party service. Links to press
        coverage lead to external websites whose accessibility we do not
        control.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
